Subject: [PATCH] Add "Dump Executable Code (.code)" to the game list (Build
 128)

Right-clicking a game now offers "Dump Executable Code (.code)", which
writes the decrypted ExeFS .code section to <user>/dump/code/<title
id>.code and opens the folder. The loader already decrypts with the
console's own keys, so nothing secret leaves the machine. It is for
reading a game's own constants (e.g. the NEX access key and game-server
ID a custom server needs) without extra tools; use it on games that
still have no game server (002-0110 in the services log). Qt frontend
only (calls AppLoader::ReadCode).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
